overview=dict(status='usable',rationale='Source-grounded navigation of normal formation, election/context change, old-work cleanup and necessary membership/recovery/application support. Usable means sufficient initial mechanism understanding for a local question, not a correctness claim or verified fault coverage.',formation=path('ApplyLog creates a command future and sends applyCh. The leader main loop rejects transfer/removal cases or assigns term/index and stores a batch. Successful local storage and successful per-peer append/snapshot paths report indices into the leader-generation commitment. Only current voter slots count; the majority index must reach the first index of this leader term. The commit notification makes the leader record commitIndex, commit configuration changes and enqueue indexed work to processLogs/runFSM. Replication requests propagate LeaderCommitIndex; followers validate previous entries, reconcile/store suffixes and apply the bounded leader commit. FSM return precedes local command future response. Heartbeats omit entries and commit index, and are not log support.', ['b-admit','b-dispatch','b-append','b-replicate','b-commit','b-consume-commit','b-fsm','b-install'],['f-append-accepted','f-match','f-commit','f-fsm-queued','f-applied'],['s-apply','s-dispatch','s-rpc','s-replication','s-pipeline','s-commitment','s-leader-loop','s-fsm']),context=path('A timed-out eligible follower becomes candidate; optional pre-vote precedes a real campaign that persists a new term/self vote and asks configured voters. RequestVote checks membership, known leader, term, saved vote and last-entry freshness. Campaign-local channels isolate old replies. Majority selects Leader; setup creates a fresh commitment object and no-op. Higher-term RPC/reply handling, insufficient recent voter contact, negative verification or committed self removal can demote. Leader exit closes worker stop channels and fails unresolved local futures; captured worker support remains attached to the old object. Transfer waits for target replication and sends TimeoutNow, whose candidate bypasses pre-vote but still seeks real votes. Restart restores term/history/configuration as Follower. Network empty-heartbeat handling can bypass the main RPC queue; it is an actual asynchronous owner, despite main-thread-only comments.', ['b-vote','b-campaign','b-leader-life','b-heartbeat','b-lease','b-verify','b-recover'],['f-vote-granted','f-leader-generation','f-contact','f-verification-notification'],['s-follower','s-election','s-campaign','s-vote','s-leader-life','s-transfer','s-startup','s-network-dispatch','s-rpc']),connection=path('Log and snapshot history survive role changes, while volatile support and client futures do not transfer to a new leader generation. New authority re-establishes index support through real replication and its current-term no-op; voter log-freshness checks connect persisted history to elections. Membership is latest-versus-committed: new leader changes wait for a committed current-term entry and stable configuration, then update voter aggregation and all-peer replication; retained voter IDs preserve their slots. Followers roll back latest configuration on suffix conflict and recover configuration from snapshot/logs. Snapshot installation supplies a prefix match only after storage/FSM restore and response processing; application queueing is distinct from completed application. VerifyLeader uses a separate Boolean notification path and must not be equated with commitment. User Restore is an explicitly restricted disaster-recovery override with aborted inflight futures and a later no-op completion.', ['b-leader-life','b-config','b-vote','b-recover','b-install','b-user-restore','b-verify'],['f-match','f-vote-granted','f-verification-notification'],['s-leader-life','s-commitment','s-repl-ownership','s-config-change','s-rpc','s-vote','s-startup','s-install','s-restore-contract']),core_gaps=[],open_details=['Network heartbeat concurrent context-write interleavings versus main loop; source comments and wiring differ.','VerifyLeader suffrage filtering, response timing and applicable authority contract need discrimination.','Heartbeat contact versus higher-term reply handling: other workers and negative verification may protect authority.','Pipeline error/partial-response semantics relative to AppendFuture.Response contract.','Automatic snapshot creation/compaction, forced RecoverCluster and store-specific crash behavior remain deferred.','No executed operation history, property evidence, or overall correctness conclusion exists.'])
